                "When I came to Renfield's room I found him lying on the floor on his left side in a glittering pool of blood. His face was horribly bruised, as though it had been beaten against the floor; indeed it was from the face wounds that the pool of blood originated. The attendant, Simmons, who was kneeling beside the body, said to me as we turned him over that he thought the poor fellow's back was broken; both the right arm and leg, and the whole side of the face, were paralysed.",
