                "I sent at once for Dr. Van Helsing, who came in dressing gown and slippers. After a strict examination we found the wounds of the face superficial; the real injury was a depressed fracture of the skull, extending right up through the motor area. 'We must trephine at once,' said the Professor, 'or it may be too late.' We expected he would recover consciousness after the operation -- for a short time, at all events -- and that his words might be worth many lives.",
